---
layout: changelog
title: Encrypted buckets now encrypt files of every size
date: 2026-11-08
cover: /images/blog/encrypting-every-file-in-appwrite-storage/cover.avif
tags: storage, security
---

[Bucket encryption](/docs/products/storage/buckets#encryption) now covers files of any size. Until now, files larger than 20 MB were stored unencrypted, even in a bucket with encryption on.

With this change:

- Each file gets its own random key and is encrypted with AES-256-GCM in 64 KB segments before it reaches storage.
- Encrypted uploads take about as long as unencrypted ones. In buckets without compression, range requests decrypt only the segments they read.
- An encrypted file now takes up about the same storage as the original, instead of about a third more.
- Files you uploaded before keep working. Files larger than 20 MB uploaded before this change stay unencrypted until you upload them again.

The change is live on Appwrite Cloud, and comes to self-hosted Appwrite in the next release. You don't need to change any code.

